      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 263,
      "text": "In Japan, this card was available as part of the Trade Please campaign that ran from February 10 to July 31, 1998. Participants were required to mail a flyer included with copies of"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 264,
      "text": "Trade Please"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 267,
      "text": "to MediaFactory along with any two Pokemon trading cards and a return envelope within the campaign period. Participants could select a \"course\" detailed on the flyer by writing in the appropriate space. The \"A Course\" included a"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 268,
      "text": "Charizard"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 269,
      "text": "card and a copy of this card. The \"B Course\" included a"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 270,
      "text": "Blastoise"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 271,
      "text": "card and a copy of this card. The \"C Course\" included a"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 272,
      "text": "Venusaur"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trade_Please!_(Trade_Please_promo)",
      "line": 273,
      "text": "card and a copy of this card. MediaFactory would then send the two cards from the chosen course to the participant, completing the trade."
    },
